  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Community Stabilization for Conflict-Affected Communities in Northern Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project contributes to promoting stabilization and preventing violent extremism in Northern Mozambique particularly in communities affected by conflict with a specific focus on youth, women, and girls. The International Organization for Migration (IOM) is conducting activities to support community-led conflict prevention and creating a conducive environment for communities to live peaceful and productive lives through income generation and improved infrastructure. By focusing on addressing root causes in a context-specific way, IOM aims to promote stability, reduce vulnerability and build local resilience - contributing to Mozambique achieving Sustainable Development Goal 16, Peace, justice and strong institutions.</narrative>
  </description>
